40
00:01:20,691 --> 00:01:22,060
Prices went up.

41
00:01:22,008 --> 00:01:23,740
Each piece of gold bought less.

42
00:01:23,754 --> 00:01:26,780
Economists have a name for this: inflation.

43
00:01:26,740 --> 00:01:28,300
And it didn't bounce back quickly.

44
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:31,980
The historian al-Umari, writing about twelve years later,

45
00:01:31,924 --> 00:01:34,540
reported that gold in Cairo still hadn't recovered

46
00:01:34,480 --> 00:01:35,500
its value.

47
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:37,820
One man's shopping trip shook the gold market

48
00:01:37,747 --> 00:01:39,100
of an entire region.

49
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,781
His fame spread all the way to Europe.

50
00:01:40,813 --> 00:01:43,820
On a famous map from 1375, the Catalan

51
